<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tancred, Prince of Galilee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1075–1112</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Tancred of Hauteville</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tancred was an Italo-Norman leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> and a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemond-i-of-antioch">Bohemond of Taranto</a>. After the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1099 he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberias">Tiberias</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> and styled himself prince there. He later ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> as regent, expanding it at the expense of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tancred-prince-of-galilee.jpg" alt="Tancred, Prince of Galilee" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tankreds_coin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Haifa was taken in August 1100 by <b>Tancred</b> with the help of a Venetian fleet, after a stubborn defence in which its Jewish and Muslim inhabitants fought together.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-haifa">Lordship of Haifa</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Tancred</b>, the Norman crusader, took Tiberias and the surrounding region soon after the capture of Jerusalem in 1099 and styled himself Prince of Galilee.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-galilee">Principality of Galilee</a></li><li><blockquote>Ridwan lost territory to the Principality of Antioch and paid tribute to <b>Tancred</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/seljuk-emirate-of-aleppo">Seljuk Emirate of Aleppo</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=36.2,36.15&amp;year=1099" aria-label="Antioch on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5460 857 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Tancred, Prince of Galilee"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5910 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5910 1127h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=36.2,36.15&amp;year=1099">What was here in 1099? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
